# Pinned from the real red run of 2026-07-29 with the injection applied.
#
# The injection restores the pre-fix daemon in both places the fix touches:
# `post_stage` persists nothing about the stage, and boot recovery drops the
# stage identity before it can reach the respawn rules. That is the defect
# exactly — a stage whose daemon restarts mid-run is rehydrated as a run, read
# as a half-recorded dispatch (a stage has a `last_path` and never a
# `stdout_path`), and left with no completion watcher at all.
exit: 101

# THE SYMPTOM, once per shared stage path. The stage's worker finalizes, the
# release is persisted — and the tx ledger is empty. `stage_outcome_from_session`
# is never called, so the stage has no terminal record of any kind. The
# assertion prints the whole ledger after the panic line, so an empty one is
# visible rather than inferred.
contains: a grill stage that is live across a daemon restart must still emit its terminal tx (grill.completed)
contains: a plan stage that is live across a daemon restart must still emit its terminal tx (plan.completed)

# `architect` specifically: its worker finalize emits `architector.reported`,
# not `architector.done` (TASK-6AYEJ.1), so a recovery keyed on a `.done` tx
# would pass the other two and still miss this one.
contains: a architect stage that is live across a daemon restart must still emit its terminal tx (architect.completed)

# THE CAUSE, on the production path: a real `POST /api/grill` leaves nothing on
# disk that says which stage this run is, so there is nothing for a restarted
# daemon to rebuild the watcher from.
#
# Re-pinned 2026-07-30 (TASK-3NJ9K). The tail used to read `session had:
# [String("acquire"), String("run_meta")]`, taken from a fixture addressed at
# `acp-stdio`/`codex`: on a host with codex installed that launch spawned `codex
# app-server`, and whether its `Ready` had reached the session before the test
# read it was a race. TASK-3NJ9K moved the fixture onto the in-process stub, so
# the list changed — and, more to the point, stopped racing. It is therefore
# pinned in full again rather than truncated: with no provider subprocess in the
# picture the phases are deterministic (measured identical across three runs),
# and a proof that stops naming what it found is a weaker proof than the one
# this task inherited.
contains: a launched stage must persist its stage identity so boot recovery can respawn the completion watcher; session had: [String("acquire"), String("run_meta"), Null]

# All four, and only these four. A binary that collapses wholesale is a
# different failure and has not reproduced this defect.
contains: test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 4 failed
